From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The opening's banners: each one's other half placed with it
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

When the opening puts its banners back at the start (ov77_021D636C), it
places one half of each; the other half, beside the DS's screen, followed
on the next frame's move. The 3DS remaster's wider screen shows that half,
so for that frame a black gap showed at the banner's end. Both halves are
placed at once now.
---
 src/game_opening/ov77_021D54B0.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/game_opening/ov77_021D54B0.c b/src/game_opening/ov77_021D54B0.c
--- a/src/game_opening/ov77_021D54B0.c
+++ b/src/game_opening/ov77_021D54B0.c
@@ -591,6 +591,12 @@ void ov77_021D636C(UnkStruct_ov77_021D5564 *param0, int param1)
     v1.x = 128 * FX32_ONE;
 
     Sprite_SetPosition(param0->unk_250[15], &v1);
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    // Each banner's other half, beside the DS's screen, put with it now
+    // rather than on the next frame's move: the 3DS remaster's wider screen
+    // shows it.
+    ov77_021D6290(param0, 0);
+#endif
 }
 
 void ov77_021D6470(UnkStruct_ov77_021D5564 *param0, int param1)
-- 
